-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Pssst
  Publisher   Ultimate Play The Game, 1983
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch
  (one of these files):

  File        Pssst (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game)[16K].tzx
  MD5         1e261de928be1dacaef513687d230ebb

  File        Pssst (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game)[16K].tap
  MD5         c609424b634d2d7a3c6e704c5bcc1327

  File        Pssst (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game)[a][16K].tzx
  MD5         27d9876d386785884fd66d0f61aa923d

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original

  Note        Robbie, his spray cans, the spray and the pests are hardware
              sprites in their own colours, laid on the pixels the game still
              draws, so a pest no longer colours the leaves, the stalk or
              Robbie as it crosses them. The flower, the leaves and the lives
              are drawn once and stay as the game draws them. Proven on
              machine-played games of the first level and on every graphic
              through the game's own draw routine; later levels are not proven
              in play. Pace: kept by design, the same method as Jet Pac 1.3;
              not measured for this game.

